     174,
     1289,
     1047,
     1418
    ],
    "block_content": "Denote $\\mathrm{var}(\\boldsymbol{c}_k^{[i]}) = \\|\\widehat{\\boldsymbol{C}}_k^{[i;]}\\|_F^2 / n$ and $\\mathrm{var}(\\boldsymbol{x}_k^{[i]}) = \\|\\widehat{\\boldsymbol{X}}_k^{[i;]}\\|_F^2 / n$. By the triangle inequality, (85), (86), $\\delta_{\\eta} = o(1)$, and $o(1) = \\delta_k \\propto \\delta_{V_k} \\sqrt{p_k}$ (from (41), (79), and $\\lambda_{k,1} \\propto \\lambda_{k,r_k}$ in Assumption 1 (ii)), we have $\\max_{i \\leq p_k} \\widehat{\\mathrm{var}}(\\boldsymbol{c}_k^{[i]}) \\leq \\|\\widehat{\\mathrm{cov}}(\\boldsymbol{c}_k)\\|_{\\max} \\lesssim_P \\lambda_{k,1} / p_k$. By (82) and $\\min_{i \\leq p_k} \\mathrm{var}(\\boldsymbol{x}_k^{[i]}) \\geq M_k \\lambda_{r_k}(\\mathrm{cov}(\\boldsymbol{x}_k)) / p_k$, we obtain $\\min_{i \\leq p_k} \\widehat{\\mathrm{var}}(\\boldsymbol{x}_k^{[i]}) \\geq M_k \\lambda_{r_k}(\\mathrm{cov}(\\boldsymbol{x}_k)) / p_k -$"
